From aebc956a224e1b5a921b38ead49725494d56f795 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Martin Mirchev <mmirchev@comp.nus.edu.sg>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:01:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] avformat/http: free the zlib state when the open fails

parse_content_encoding() initialises the inflate stream as soon as a
Content-Encoding: gzip or deflate header is read. If the open fails
after that, e.g. because the connection ends before the end of the
headers, http_close() is not called and the stream is never freed:
LeakSanitizer reports 7160 bytes per failed open.

Call inflateEnd() in the error path of http_open(). inflateEnd() is a
no-op on a stream that was never initialised.

Reported in the review of #25635.

Signed-off-by: Martin Mirchev <mmirchev@comp.nus.edu.sg>
(cherry picked from commit aebc956a224e1b5a921b38ead49725494d56f795)
---
 libavformat/http.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libavformat/http.c b/libavformat/http.c
index afe99afef4d1..be73b7da065b 100644
--- a/libavformat/http.c
+++ b/libavformat/http.c
@@ -860,6 +860,9 @@ static int http_open(URLContext *h, const char *uri, int flags,
     ret = http_open_cnx(h, options, 0);
 bail_out:
     if (ret < 0) {
+#if CONFIG_ZLIB
+        inflateEnd(&s->inflate_stream);
+#endif
         av_dict_free(&s->chained_options);
         av_dict_free(&s->cookie_dict);
         av_dict_free(&s->redirect_cache);
